{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"cef97b76-b037-4aa1-bb33-ccc90fcca459","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have investigated why the nightly job never reported anything and resolved the issue.\n\n### Root Causes\n\n1. **Why `claude` failed:**\n   As seen in [`Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`](file:///tmp/h-4iRz6I/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err), Claude Code exited with `Not logged in · Please run /login` because it lacked valid session credentials or an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in the launchd environment.\n\n2. **Why no failure notification was sent over Telegram:**\n   In [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-4iRz6I/bin/nightly-review.zsh), line 19 attempted `status=$?`. In `zsh`, `status` is a special built-in, read-only variable aliased to `$?`. Attempting to assign to it triggered a fatal error (`read-only variable: status`), causing the script to terminate immediately before calling [`bin/notify.sh`](file:///tmp/h-4iRz6I/bin/notify.sh) on lines 21–23.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n- Updated [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-4iRz6I/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L24) to use `exit_code` instead of the reserved variable `status`. Now failure notifications are properly routed to Telegram.\n- Documented the full analysis, causes, and recommendations for Claude authentication in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-4iRz6I/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":136.130801,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":230485,"output_tokens":3098,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":588875,"total_tokens":233583}}}
